## 5. Auth setup & how `ctx.authentication` / `organizationId` are derived

### `apps/worker/src/middleware/context.ts:21-68` — initializes `db` + `betterAuth` instance on every request
`contextMiddleware` sets `c.set("db", ...)` and `c.set("betterAuth", auth)`. `AuthType` (line 76-79) = `{ user: $Infer.Session.user; session: $Infer.Session.session }`.

### `apps/worker/src/middleware/auth.ts:14-27` — HTTP-route auth guard
```ts
14: export const enforceAuthMiddleware = createMiddleware<EnforcedAuthHonoEnv>(async (c, next) => {
15: 	const betterAuth = c.get("betterAuth");
16: 	const session = await betterAuth.api.getSession({ headers: c.req.raw.headers });
17: 	if (!session?.user || !session?.session) {
18: 		throw new HTTPException(401, { message: "Unauthorized" });
19: 	}
20: 	c.set("authentication", session);
21: 	await next();
22: });
```

### tRPC context — `apps/worker/src/trpc/server.ts:6-23` (this is what tRPC procedures actually see)
```ts
6: export const trpcServer = honoTrpcServer({
7: 	router: trpcRouter,
8: 	createContext: async (_opts, c: Context<HonoEnv>) => {
9: 		const betterAuth = c.get("betterAuth");
10: 		const authentication = await betterAuth.api.getSession({
11: 			headers: c.req.raw.headers,
12: 		});
13: 		return {
14: 			authentication,
15: 			db: c.get("db"),
16: 			betterAuth,
17: 			userAssets: c.get("userAssets"),
18: 			env: c.env,
19: 			waitUntil: c.executionCtx.waitUntil.bind(c.executionCtx),
20: 			headers: c.req.raw.headers,
21: 		};
22: 	},
23: });
```
`organizationId` is **never a header** — it is always `authentication.session.activeOrganizationId`, injected by middleware in `trpc.ts`. The session is resolved from the request headers (cookie, or **bearer token** — the worker mounts the `bearer()` plugin at `better-auth.ts:328` and `expo()` at line 274, so mobile bearer-token auth already works with this same context).

Mounting: `apps/worker/src/index.ts:29-37` — `/api/auth` (better-auth REST, where `setActive` lives), `/api/trpc/*` (tRPC), then `enforceAuthMiddleware` for everything else.

