## 6. Existing hooks

There are **no `useActiveLeague` / `useOrganizations` custom hooks**. The app uses better-auth's React hooks directly, plus one session wrapper:

| Hook/Pattern | Where |
|---|---|
| `useSession()` (custom React Query wrapper over `authClient.getSession`) | `apps/web/src/hooks/useSession.ts:10-22` (also `useSessionInvalidate` line 28, `fetchSessionForRoute` line 40) |
| `authClient.useListOrganizations()` | app-sidebar.tsx:50, index.tsx:45, accept-invitation:36 |
| `authClient.useSession()` | app-sidebar.tsx:49, accept-invitation:35 |
| `authClient.useActiveMember()` (role in active org) | app-sidebar.tsx:51, plus 8 league pages |
| `useQuery(trpc.league.list.queryOptions())` | `_authenticated/leagues/index.tsx:21`, `_sidebar/profile.tsx:73` |

The closest thing to a "useActiveLeague" pattern is inline in `app-sidebar.tsx:78-90` (shown in §1): derive `activeOrg` from `session.session.activeOrganizationId` + `useListOrganizations()`, then build `{ id, name, slug, logo }` for the `LeagueSwitcher`.

